<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Rakwa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1007</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Rakwa was an Umayyad pretender who led a major revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> from 1004 to 1006. Claiming descent from the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, he won over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> and Arab tribes in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> and defeated Fatimid armies before advancing into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. Defeated near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giza">Giza</a> in 1006, he fled south towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, was handed over by the chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kanz">Banu Kanz</a> and was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> in 1007.</p></div>
